<title>FRANCE: MATIF May financial contracts volume fell 0.1 pct.</title>
<headline>MATIF May financial contracts volume fell 0.1 pct.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-06-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>The volume of financial futures and options contracts traded on the French MATIF exchange in May fell 0.1 percent from the previous month but rose 41.8 percent compared to May 1996, Matif said in a statement on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Detailed figures for financial contracts were as follows:</p>
<p>			   Volume     Change    Change  Open positions</p>
<p>					 on month   on year  at end-month</p>
<p> All contracts	6.48 bln   -0.1 pct   +41.8 pct  1.26 bln</p>
<p>  Financial futures 4.99 bln   -5.4 pct   +31.9 pct   580,737</p>
<p>Of which:</p>
<p>     -  French bond 2.91 bln   -3.8 pct   +19.6 pct   216,827</p>
<p>     -  PIBOR	 1.49 bln  -11.9 pct   +81.0 pct   285,677</p>
<p>     -  CAC-40	 555,453   +6.7 pct   +16.3 pct    72,387</p>
<p>     -  Ecu bond	30,408   -1.0 pct   -34.4 pct     5,762</p>
<p>     -  Bobl		 130     -	     -		 79</p>
<p>     -  LYS		    5     -	     -		  5</p>
<p>  Financial options 1.49 bln  +23.0 pct   +89.9 pct   681,599</p>
<p>Of which:</p>
<p>     -  French bond  995,106  +16.3 pct   +60.4 pct   235,508</p>
<p>     -  PIBOR	  486,077  +38.1 pct   +21.6 pct   440,150</p>
<p>     -  Bobl	     4,002     -	     -	    3,400</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom +331 4221 5542</p>
